preConditionHook:
// EL: rangeLow = lowest(low, lookback), rangeHigh = highest(high, lookback),
// the window INCLUSIVE of the current bar as the source states it. Buy the
// bottom of the range, sell the top -- a fade with no reversal-bar
// requirement.
//
// Highest/Lowest bottom out in EL's Extremes(), which is EL SOURCE: seeded at
// the window's first bar, scanning the rest, STRICT comparison so a tie keeps
// the earliest bar; being EL source, its relational operator carries the same
// 2.22e-12 tolerance, hence el_lt/el_gt in the scan.
//
// The condition is the MULTIPLIED form of the stochastic ratio
// (close - LL) / (HH - LL) <= bottomFraction. Written that way so an N-bar
// block of identical bars cannot divide by zero -- EasyLanguage raises a
// RUNTIME divide-by-zero error on a zero denominator -- and so no epsilon
// input is needed. Degenerate case HH == LL: 0 <= 0, both sides fire, which is
// the honest reading of a range with no height.
//
// Not CloseRangePosition, which places the close inside the CURRENT BAR's own
// range. Not ClosePercentileRank, which ranks the close among the last N
// CLOSES by counting -- this reads the high-low envelope, so wicks move it and
// not the rank. Not RangeMidpointZone, which is a band around the midpoint.
rangeLow = low[0];
rangeHigh = high[0];
for (int i = 1; i < (int)lookback; ++i) {
    if (el_lt(low[i], rangeLow)) rangeLow = low[i];
    if (el_gt(high[i], rangeHigh)) rangeHigh = high[i];
}
